	{
		local_m02 = ask(local_m08);
		// X: reconstructed repeated-string selection; authored switch versus if ladder is unproved.
		switch local_m02
		{
			case "Are they not all the same? "
			{
				bark("Indeed, no, although many people use -- or should I say misuse -- the word `Pagan' to mean the world, the island, and, for a few ethnocentrics, the city. In actuality, Pagan is only the name for the world. ");
				local_m08 -= <<"Are they not all the same? ">>;
			}
			case "Actually, I meant the people. "
			{
				bark("To be honest, I know little about the people. A few come to visit me for my knowledge. And even fewer to buy my scrolls. I do know a little about the mages of Pagan. Is it them you are interested in knowing? ");
				mythranScrolls = 1;
				local_m08 -= <<"Are they not all the same? ", "Actually, I meant the people. ">>;
				local_m08 ^= <<"Tell me of the mages. ", "You sell scrolls? ">>;
			}
			case "Tell me of the mages. "
			{
				local_m08 -= <<"Tell me of the mages. ">>;
				bark("There are four of what I call 'schools' of magic on Pagan -- one for each of the Titans. The study of death and the ground is called Necromancy. It is the Necromancer who is responsible for carrying out the pact with Lithos by burying the dead and sending their spirits to him. ");
				if lothianDead
				{
					bark("The current Necromancer, Vividos, is fairly new to his position. This means that he has been away from the city for only a few years, and is, therefore, less reclusive. In time, however, he will have forgotten most of his social graces, and the people will find dealing with him as distasteful as they did his predecessors. ");
				}
				else
				{
					bark("The current Necromancer, Lothian, is very old. I expect she soon will be passing her role to her Apprentice. Vividos should handle the responsibility quite well. ");
				}
				bark("Tempestry's main focus is water, though its aspect does involve combining with Hydros' sister Titan, Stratos, making storms as much a part of Tempestry as is the sea. Unlike the other schools, Tempestry is not learned. It is passed on through the bloodline. The eldest living Tempest possesses the greatest amount of power. However, as long as a younger Tempest's spell does not contradict an elder's, the younger's magic will work fully. ");
				if devonInRule
				{
					bark("Since there seems to be little cap on the powers of Tempestry, I am glad for the Pagans that Devon now rules Tenebrae. You should be commended for your role in that. ");
				}
				else
				{
					bark("Since there seems to be little cap on the powers of Tempestry, it is a true tragedy that Mordea rules the city. I hope for the sake of the people that her reign is not a long one. ");
				}
				bark("Stellos was the first follower of Stratos. His Order of Enlightenment teaches Theurgy, the study of the winds. He is a good and learned man, if you will permit me a judgement of ethics, who freely uses his powers of healing. ");
				bark("The fourth school, Sorcery, involves the Titan of Fire. I have never spoken to Malchir in person, but I feel the Sorcerers' reputation for deceit is unchanged by his rise to power. Take care when dealing with those who consort with Pyros, for it seems they become as wicked as he. ");
				bark("Those are the mages of the four schools. Of course, they do not represent -all- aspects of magic on Pagan. ");
				local_m08 ^= <<"What other magic exists? ">>;
			}
			case "What other magic exists? "
			{
				local_m08 -= <<"What other magic exists? ">>;
				bark("There is what I call Thaumaturgy. It is not tied to any of the Titans, but borrows bits and pieces from any form of magic you can imagine. I am a practitioner of Thaumaturgy. ");
				local_m08 ^= <<"Can you teach me Thaumaturgy? ">>;
				mythMagic = 1;
			}
			case "Can you teach me Thaumaturgy? "
			{
				local_m08 -= <<"Can you teach me Thaumaturgy? ">>;
